 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "This is my poor heart's life, o'er sixty years,\nThe love I had for thee; it has given\nTo me this love and sorrow.\nVI. Now the war-souls that sleep upon\nAll earths' air do weep on the death thereof,\nFor ever: their restless spirits above\nFell silent in their graves to heaven.\nIt was not love enough for them seven;\nThey knew what happiness is above,\nThat each has a meaning thereof,\nA doom as one by reason set,\nIn which he moves nevermore again.",
